<Layout title="Learning & resources"><PageIntro eyebrow="Knowledge is something we share" title="A little understanding. New possibilities." description="Explore the ideas behind regenerative growing, and continue learning with the wider community." /><section class="section container article-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>What is permaculture?</h2><p>Permaculture is an approach to designing human systems with lessons from nature. It connects care for the Earth, care for people, and responsible sharing of resources. A garden is one expression of it; community organization, water use, and learning can be others.</p><h2>What is agroforestry?</h2><p>Agroforestry brings trees together with crops or other agricultural activities. A diverse planting can support food production, soil health, habitat, and resilience when it is designed for local conditions.</p><h2>What is a food forest?</h2><p>A food forest is a way of growing food using a woodland-like structure: different plants occupy different layers and roles. It may combine fruit trees, shrubs, herbs, and ground-cover plants.</p><h2>What makes an approach regenerative?</h2><p>Regenerative approaches aim to renew the health of living systems: soils, biodiversity, water, and the relationships that communities depend on. Outcomes depend on place, practice, and sustained care.</p><h2>Keep learning.</h2><ul><li><a href="https://agroforestryrc.org/videos/">ARC’s videos and learning materials</a> introduce work across its agroforestry network.</li><li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCgcHJJZKJlrqwrCCMjIRHCg">AEF’s YouTube channel</a> provides a starting point for its published media.</li><li><a href="https://www.thepermaculturepodcast.com/">The Permaculture Podcast</a> explores practitioners, ideas, and community experience.</li><li><a href="https://sdgs.un.org/goals">UN Sustainable Development Goals</a> offer a broader framework referenced in AEF’s archived applications.</li></ul><p class="source-note">External resources are maintained by their respective publishers. They may have their own data and cookie policies.</p></div><aside class="aside-card"><h3>See the ideas in practice.</h3><p>Explore documented examples of food growing, education, and local resilience.</p><a class="button" href="/projects/">Explore projects <Icon /></a></aside></section><Newsletter /></Layout>
